llapsibleButton_M8p5">On this page</button></div><div class=3D"theme-doc-ma=
rkdown markdown"><h1>Environments <span class=3D"badge_jWvi" role=3D"status=
" aria-label=3D"The following section contains beta content">Beta</span></h=
1>
<p>1Password Environments provide the ability to store, organize, and manag=
e project secrets in the form of environment variables from a dedicated loc=
ation in 1Password. This creates a simplified process for accessing and syn=
cing developer credentials stored in 1Password in development contexts and =
with other platforms. Each environment is self-contained, giving you the fl=
exibility to organize your secrets by project, stage, application, or your =
own convention.</p>
<p>Use environments to import existing <code>.env</code> files, create an i=
ntuitive onboarding experience for your team to manage secrets, and more.</=
p>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_Iu3P" id=3D"requirements">Requir=
ements<a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/#require=
ments" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Requirements" title=
=3D"Direct link to Requirements">=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<p>Before you can use Environments, you'll need to:</p>
<ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://1password.com/pricing/password-manager" target=3D"_b=
lank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">Sign up for 1Password</a>.</li>
<li>Install and sign in to 1Password for <a href=3D"https://1password.com/d=
ownloads/mac" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">Mac</a>, <a hre=
f=3D"https://1password.com/downloads/windows" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noop=
ener noreferrer">Windows</a>, or <a href=3D"https://1password.com/downloads=
/linux" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer">Linux</a>. <br><small=
>This feature is not available in 1Password for iOS or Android.</small></li=
>
<li>Have <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/#turn=
-on-1password-developer">1Password Developer turned on</a>.</li>
</ul>
<h3 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_Iu3P" id=3D"turn-on-1password-de=
veloper">Turn on 1Password Developer<a href=3D"https://developer.1password.=
com/docs/environments/#turn-on-1password-developer" class=3D"hash-link" ari=
a-label=3D"Direct link to Turn on 1Password Developer" title=3D"Direct link=
 to Turn on 1Password Developer">=E2=80=8B</a></h3>
<ol>
<li>Open and unlock the 1Password desktop app.</li>
<li>Select your account or collection at the top of the sidebar and choose =
<strong>Settings</strong> &gt; <a href=3D"onepassword://settings/developers=
" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noopener noreferrer"><strong>Developer</strong><=
/a>.</li>
<li>Turn on <strong>Show 1Password Developer experience</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_Iu3P" id=3D"create-an-environmen=
t">Create an environment<a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/env=
ironments/#create-an-environment" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct =
link to Create an environment" title=3D"Direct link to Create an environmen=
t">=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<ol>
<li>In the 1Password desktop app, go to <strong>Developer</strong> &gt; <st=
rong>View Environments</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>New environment</strong>.</li>
<li>Enter a name for the new environment, then select <strong>Save</strong>=
. If you have multiple 1Password accounts, you can select which account to =
save the environment to.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_Iu3P" id=3D"manage-an-environmen=
t">Manage an environment<a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/env=
ironments/#manage-an-environment" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct =
link to Manage an environment" title=3D"Direct link to Manage an environmen=
t">=E2=80=8B</a></h3>
<p>If you want to rename or remove an environment, select <strong>Manage En=
vironment</strong> from within that environment. Choose <strong>Rename envi=
ronment</strong> or <strong>Delete environment</strong> as needed.</p>
<p>Deleted environments cannot be restored and any associated integrations =
will stop working. 1Password will prompt you to confirm whether or not you =
want to delete your environment before proceeding.</p>
<h4 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_Iu3P" id=3D"add-or-remove-users-=
to-an-environment">Add or remove users to an environment<a href=3D"https://=
developer.1password.com/docs/environments/#add-or-remove-users-to-an-enviro=
nment" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Add or remove users=
 to an environment" title=3D"Direct link to Add or remove users to an envir=
onment">=E2=80=8B</a></h4>
<p>If you're using a shared account, such as for a team or business, you ca=
n share environments with team members. Each environment remains independen=
t, allowing you to work across multiple environments in different accounts =
while keeping environment variables separate. Access must be granted for ea=
ch environment.</p>
<ol>
<li>From your environment, select <strong>Manage environment</strong> &gt; =
<strong>Manage access</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>Add People</strong>, then search for and select the user=
 you want to add to the environment. Select <strong>Next</strong>.</li>
<li>Select <strong>View &amp; Edit</strong>, and choose whether the user ca=
n view, edit, and or manage the environment.</li>
<li>To remove a user from an environment, return to that user on the "Manag=
e access" screen and select <strong>Remove from environment</strong>.</li>
</ol>
<h3 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_Iu3P" id=3D"add-variables">Add v=
ariables<a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/#add-v=
ariables" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Add variables" t=
itle=3D"Direct link to Add variables">=E2=80=8B</a></h3>
<p>Variables are where key-value pairs are stored within 1Password Environm=
ents. From the Environments screen, select <strong>View environment</strong=
> for the environment you want to add variables for.</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p>If you have an existing <code>.env</code> file with the variable informa=
tion you want to add to the Environment, select <strong>Import.env file</st=
rong>. The information will automatically fill into the correct fields.</p>
</li>
<li>
<p>To manually add environment variables, select <strong>New variable</stro=
ng>. Enter your key-value pair information to the <strong>Name</strong> and=
 <strong>Value</strong> fields.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>Select <strong>New variable</strong> to add additional key-value pairs t=
o the same environment.</p>
<p>Values are hidden by default, but you can toggle the visibility on or of=
f in the <strong>Actions</strong> column. You can also delete variables fro=
m this column. Select <strong>Edit</strong> within the environment to add, =
edit, or delete variables at a later time.</p>
<p>After you've added variables to an environment, you can use the Action c=
olumn on the Variables screen within your environment to quickly copy your =
values without revealing them. Or, you can choose to reveal them.</p>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_Iu3P" id=3D"destinations">Destin=
ations<a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/#destina=
tions" class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Destinations" title=
=3D"Direct link to Destinations">=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<p>Destinations are the places where you can use the variables in your envi=
ronments. Right now, you can <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/doc=
s/environments/aws-secrets-manager">sync environment variables to AWS Secre=
ts Manager</a> or use <a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/envir=
onments/local-env-file">local <code>.env</code> file mounting</a> as a dest=
ination.</p>
<p>You can view, add, or edit destinations from the <strong>Destination</st=
rong> tab within your environment. You might also need to configure setting=
s within your destination.</p>
<h2 class=3D"anchor anchorWithStickyNavbar_Iu3P" id=3D"learn-more">Learn mo=
re<a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/#learn-more"=
 class=3D"hash-link" aria-label=3D"Direct link to Learn more" title=3D"Dire=
ct link to Learn more">=E2=80=8B</a></h2>
<ul>
<li><a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/aws-secret=
s-manager">Sync secrets between 1Password and AWS Secrets Manager (beta)</a=
></li>
<li><a href=3D"https://developer.1password.com/docs/environments/local-env-=
file">Access secrets from 1Password through local <code>.env</code> files</=
a></li>
</ul></div></article><nav class=3D"pagination-nav docusaurus-mt-lg" aria-la=
